# Requests for the local MLX model server, for the VS Code REST Client extension
# (humao.rest-client). Start the server first with the "Start MLX Model Server"
# Raycast command, then click "Send Request" above any request below.
#
# mlx_lm.server serves only the model it was started with, so "model" is omitted.
# max_tokens defaults low, so each request sets it.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1

### Check the server is up (200 OK; the model list is empty because the model
### is loaded from a local path rather than the Hugging Face cache)
GET {{base}}/models

### Simple chat
POST {{base}}/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Explain what a JWS is in two sentences." }
  ],
  "max_tokens": 300
}

### Chat with a system prompt and sampling settings
POST {{base}}/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [
    { "role": "system", "content": "You are a concise senior .NET engineer. Answer with code where helpful." },
    { "role": "user", "content": "How do I compare two byte arrays in constant time in C#?" }
  ],
  "max_tokens": 500,
  "temperature": 0.2,
  "top_p": 0.9
}

### Multi-turn conversation (paste earlier replies in as assistant messages)
POST {{base}}/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Suggest a name for a webhook receiver service." },
    { "role": "assistant", "content": "How about \"Rhizomorph\"?" },
    { "role": "user", "content": "Why might that name suit it?" }
  ],
  "max_tokens": 300
}

### Streaming (REST Client shows the raw server-sent event chunks once the stream ends)
POST {{base}}/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Count from 1 to 10, one number per line." }
  ],
  "max_tokens": 100,
  "stream": true
}

### Plain text completion (no chat template)
POST {{base}}/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prompt": "The three primary colours are",
  "max_tokens": 50
}
